  ],
  "text": "Every distant galaxy is moving away from us, and the further away it is, the faster it goes. Which sounds like we are at the centre of something. We are not. We know they are receding because their light arrives stretched towards red. It is the same effect as a siren dropping in pitch, applied to light instead of sound. But they are not flying through space away from us. Space itself is getting bigger. Picture raisins in a rising loaf. Every raisin sees every other raisin moving away. And the further apart two of them are, the more dough is expanding between them. No raisin is the centre. There is no centre in the loaf at all. So the galaxies are not moving. The distance between them is being made. Everything is running away from everything, and nobody anywhere is standing still. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
